# Interaction Design Standards (2026)

All interactive elements must meet these requirements.

## Required for every clickable element

- **Hover**: Visible feedback (opacity, color, or transform). Use `transition` with `var(--transition-fast)` or `0.2s ease`.
- **Active/pressed**: `:active` state — e.g. `transform: translateY(0)` to reverse hover lift, or `scale(0.98)`.
- **Focus-visible**: Global `*:focus-visible` in site-overrides.css covers this. Do not override with `outline: none` without providing alternative.
- **cursor: pointer**: Explicit on buttons, links, and any element with `onclick` or `role="button"`.

## Use design tokens

```css
/* Use from tokens.css */
transition: opacity var(--transition-fast);
transition: background-color var(--transition-std);
color: var(--color-terracotta-deep);  /* hover/pressed states */
```

## prefers-reduced-motion

Any decorative motion (image zoom on hover, CTA lift, hero fade) must have a `@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)` override that removes or disables it. Site-overrides.css includes a block for common elements — extend it when adding new animated components.

## CTA pattern (terracotta buttons)

```css
.cta-btn {
  transition: background-color 0.3s ease, transform 0.3s ease;
}
.cta-btn:hover {
  background-color: var(--color-terracotta-deep);
  transform: translateY(-1px);
}
.cta-btn:active {
  transform: translateY(0);
}
```
